      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "I tried this, then tried AudioX and then came back to this.\n\nI found it works best with prompts but does not keep time or follow the visual very well in most cases. Easy things like trains work great.\n\nI also found no punching or fight worked well\n\nI did use it to build the ambience in the video Footprints In Eternity and ran it using python to batch process 120 clips with captions to drive it, but only some of them worked. I then manually fed it as I went through each one in Reaper DAW where I added reverb, eq, dynamics and stretched the times where needed.\n\nI only saved the audio out, because I lined it up in Reaper after, but you can save the video with audio included just switch the \"Save output\" option on in the video out.\n\nmore about the process can be found on MarkDKBerry.com "
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
